course: dictionary
lesson: 12696
title: Abbreviations and context: DMD
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An abbreviation is a short form of longer words or names. People often make one from the first letters, like DMD. Capital letters are a common sign that a word is an abbreviation.
explain: One short form can stand for different things, so you need context to know which one is meant. «Ben's cousin has DMD, and his muscles get weaker over time.» The words muscles and weaker are the clue: here DMD is an illness.
explain: «Maya Brooks, DMD, cleaned my teeth at the clinic.» The name comes before DMD, and the word teeth is the clue. Here DMD means a qualified dentist. Always read the words around the abbreviation before you decide what it means.
fact: An abbreviation is a shortened form of a word or name, often made from first letters.
fact: DMD stands for Duchenne muscular dystrophy, a rare illness passed on in families.
fact: Duchenne muscular dystrophy is found mostly in boys, and the muscles slowly get weaker.
fact: After a dentist's name, mainly in the USA, DMD stands for Doctor of Dental Medicine.
fact: Context decides the meaning: check the words around DMD, such as muscles, teeth or research.
exercise: «Ben's cousin has DMD, and his muscles get weaker over time.» What does DMD stand for in this sentence? | Doctor of Dental Medicine | Digital micromirror device | *Duchenne muscular dystrophy | Dad's Morning Dance
exercise: «Maya Brooks, DMD, cleaned my teeth at the clinic.» What does DMD mean here? | Duchenne muscular dystrophy | *Doctor of Dental Medicine | A type of football kit
exercise: Which of these is an abbreviation? | Muscle | *DMD | Weaker | Clinic
test: «Our school raised money for DMD research at the charity walk.» What is DMD probably about here? | *An illness that weakens muscles, which people research | A school sports team | A dentist's qualification on a sign | A part of a projector
test: How are abbreviations usually written? | *Often in capital letters, like DMD | Only in numbers | Always in red ink | In small letters, like dmd
exam: Read «Dr Lee, DMD, checked her teeth.» Which meaning fits best, and what clue helps you? | A charity walk for research | Duchenne muscular dystrophy, because the word doctor means an illness | *Doctor of Dental Medicine, because the name comes before DMD and the word teeth is the clue | Digital micromirror device, because teeth are in a projector
